## Why This Is Asked
Prompts candidates to design CKNE-driven admission control and fairness in real-time multi-tenant streams, a practical production concern.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE signals to compute per-tenant health
- Dynamic rate limiting and cross-tenant shedding
- Payload schema for health metadata and token updates
- Minute-level control loop with smoothing

## Code Example

```javascript
function healthScore(p95Latency, errRate, queueDepth){
  const normLat = Math.min(p95Latency / 1000, 1);
  const normErr = Math.min(errRate, 1);
  const normQ = Math.min(queueDepth / 1000, 1);
  // Weighted mix: latency matters more
  return 0.55 * normLat + 0.25 * normErr + 0.20 * normQ;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test tail latency and fairness under correlated bursts?
- How would you handle tenants with bursty, short-lived traffic without starving others?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design CKNE-based gatekeeping in an ingestion path, ensuring per-tenant isolation, dynamic throughput control, and fidelity under load. It also probes payload design and test planning across streaming components.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE health at edge driving per-tenant gating
- Throughput controls: batch size, forwardRaw vs enriched, backpressure
- Minute-by-minute control loop for adaptive decisions
- Payload schemas: TenantCKNEHeader, RawEvent, EnrichedEvent
- Test plan: load, degradation, SLA adherence, and data fidelity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal gating decision based on CKNE and SLA
function decideForward(tenant, ckne, inFlight, sla) {
  const degraded = ckne.overall < 0.7;
  const batch = degraded ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(tenant.baseBatch * 0.5)) : tenant.baseBatch;
  const forwardRaw = !degraded || sla === 'premium';
  return { batch, forwardRaw };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the minute-by-minute loop under micro-bursts and backpressure?
- What metrics and alerting would you attach to CKNE gates at each hop?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-driven incentives in streaming, including how CKNE affects throughput, partitioning, and latency, plus a stable rebalancing loop and end-to-end validation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput/partition mapping
- Kafka partition rebalancing and windowing impact
- Baseline SLA guarantees with dynamic prioritization
- Telemetry, monitoring, and stability guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-mapping for CKNE-driven resource allocation
function mapCKNETokens(ckne, baseThroughput, basePartitions, kappa, lambda, minP, maxP){
  const T = baseThroughput * (1 + kappa * (ckne - 0.5));
  const P = Math.max(minP, Math.min(maxP, Math.round(basePartitions * (1 + lambda * (ckne - 0.5)))));
  return {throughput: T, partitions: P};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant degradation control in real-time multi-hop pipelines under load.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant circuit-breakers and edge state
- Minute-by-minute control loops with queue depth and SLA awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example control logic sketch (pseudo)
type TenantState = { id:string; ckne:string; queue:number; sla:'high'|'medium'|'low'; mode:'OPEN'|'HALF'|'CLOSED' };
function tick(states:TenantState[]) {
  for (const s of states){
    const th = s.sla==='high'? 100: s.sla==='medium'? 60: 40;
    if (s.ckne === 'red' || s.queue > th) s.mode = 'OPEN';
    else if (s.ckne === 'yellow') s.mode = 'HALF';
    else s.mode = 'CLOSED';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE-to-quotas mapping, token-based fairness, and SLA guarantees in a real-world multi-tenant dispatch scenario.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-quotas mapping
- Token-bucket with a global minute cap
- Minute-by-minute reallocation and carryover
- SLA baseline with priority to high-CKNE tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocateQuotas(totalCap, tenants) {
  const sumCKNE = tenants.reduce((s,t)=>s+t.ckne,0) || 1;
  return tenants.map(t => {
    const q = Math.floor(totalCap * (t.ckne / sumCKNE));
    return {tenant: t.tenant, quota: Math.max(1, q)};
  });
}
```

